Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 18:30:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] pack_nup: a standalone update is the whole game

A NUP may hold a game as one update package flagged STANDALONE ("an update in a
container without a base") with no base package at all: Donkey Kong Bananza
v458752 and Mario Kart World v917504 come that way, their updates carrying the
complete ExeFS and RomFS. scan() refused them ("no base game"). It now takes
an empty placeholder base, as for a dump whose update holds the whole game
(Pokemon Pokopia's v655360), and the update's own ExeFS and RomFS run.
Donkey Kong Bananza then builds and runs on the Mac (75 s, no red lines).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: NUPs that hold the whole game as one STANDALONE update with no base package (Donkey Kong Bananza v458752, Mario Kart World v917504) were refused as 'no base game'
Issue: HachebeDLC/NX2Apple#1

---
 scripts/pack_nup.py | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/scripts/pack_nup.py b/scripts/pack_nup.py
index 59a378f..2986c2a 100644
--- a/scripts/pack_nup.py
+++ b/scripts/pack_nup.py
@@ -14,7 +14,7 @@
 # Every file read is checked against its SHA-256. A repeat run keeps code modules whose content is the same and an image made from the same container tree by the same packer.
 # Needs the zstd module: compression.zstd (Python 3.14+) or backports.zstd, as the NSP script.
 # Usage: pack_nup.py <game.nup> [--version N] [--work-dir DIR]   (exit 1 on error)
-import argparse, hashlib, mmap, os, shutil, struct, sys
+import argparse, hashlib, mmap, os, shutil, struct, sys, types
 from pathlib import Path
 sys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1] / 'dm/tools'))
 import romfs_image
@@ -175,6 +175,11 @@ def is_nup(path):
 def scan(n):
     """What a NUP holds: (title ID, base package, {update version: package}, {DLC title ID: package}), with the checks pack_dump.scan makes"""
     bases = [k for k in n.packages if k.kind == BASE]
+    if not bases and any(k.kind == UPDATE and k.flags & STANDALONE and k.exefs != NO_DIR for k in n.packages):
+        # A container of a standalone update (package flag STANDALONE) holds the whole game in that update: the base is then an empty placeholder, as a dump's
+        # (Pokemon Pokopia's v655360), and the update's own ExeFS and RomFS are what runs
+        bases = [types.SimpleNamespace(nup=n, index=-1, title_id=0, root=NO_DIR, exefs=NO_DIR, romfs=NO_DIR, version=0, kind=BASE, flags=0, meta_off=0, meta_size=0,
+                                       name=f'{n.path.name} (no base: standalone update)', meta=lambda: {})]
     if not bases:
         raise Error(f'{n.path}: no base game, only ' + (', '.join(sorted({KINDS[k.kind] for k in n.packages}))) + ' packages: pack the base game and its update into one NUP')
     base = bases[0]
